# Sync local and GitHub

When an update is finished, the local repository and GitHub must match before the turn ends.

- Local copy: `D:\Google\XtraPOS` on branch `main`.
- GitHub: `origin` `https://github.com/saleem861/XtraPOS.git`.
- Commit the update, then `git push` to `origin`. Do not leave the update only in the working tree.
- Do not commit secrets: `.ssh`, `.env`, passwords, tokens, or `staging.env`.
- Do not force-push. Do not change git config. Do not skip hooks.
- A staging or production deploy is a separate request. Syncing GitHub does not deploy the site.
- If the push fails, say that GitHub was not updated. Do not claim the two copies match.
